<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>${project_name} Distribution Notes</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #0b1020;
      --panel: rgba(10, 16, 32, 0.88);
      --panel-alt: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.78);
      --line: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);
      --text: #e5edf7;
      --muted: #9db0ca;
      --accent: #4ade80;
      --accent-2: #38bdf8;
      --accent-3: #a78bfa;
      --accent-4: #f59e0b;
      --shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(2, 6, 23, 0.45);
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      font-family: "Segoe UI Variable Display", "Aptos", "Trebuchet MS", sans-serif;
      color: var(--text);
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top left, rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.18), transparent 28%),
        radial-gradient(circle at top right, rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.12), transparent 24%),
        linear-gradient(160deg, #060913 0%, #0b1020 48%, #121a30 100%);
    }

    main {
      width: min(1040px, calc(100% - 32px));
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 40px 0 56px;
    }

    .hero,
    .section {
      background: var(--panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 24px;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
    }

    .hero {
      padding: 36px;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .hero::after {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      inset: auto -120px -120px auto;
      width: 280px;
      height: 280px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.24), rgba(245, 158, 11, 0));
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
      padding: 8px 14px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.12);
      border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.2);
      color: var(--accent-2);
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 18px 0 8px;
      font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 4.2rem);
      line-height: 0.95;
    }

    .tagline {
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      color: #f8fafc;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .subtitle,
    .lead,
    li,
    .card p,
    .footer {
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.72;
    }

    .subtitle {
      max-width: 780px;
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 1.06rem;
    }

    .buttons {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 28px;
    }

    .button {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      min-width: 170px;
      padding: 12px 18px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      transition: transform 140ms ease, box-shadow 140ms ease, border-color 140ms ease;
    }

    .button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-1px);
    }

    .button-primary {
      color: #07111f;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), #86efac);
      box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.18);
    }

    .button-secondary {
      color: var(--text);
      background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.72);
      border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.24);
    }

    .stats,
    .feature-grid,
    .doc-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
      gap: 16px;
    }

    .stats {
      margin-top: 22px;
    }

    .section {
      margin-top: 22px;
      padding: 28px 30px;
    }

    .section-header {
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }

    h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--accent-4);
    }

    h3 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      color: #f8fafc;
      font-size: 1.02rem;
    }

    .lead {
      margin: 10px 0 0;
      max-width: 820px;
    }

    .card,
    .feature-group,
    .doc-column {
      padding: 18px;
      border-radius: 18px;
      background: var(--panel-alt);
      border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.16);
    }

    .card strong,
    .feature-group strong,
    .doc-column strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      color: #f8fafc;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    ol,
    ul {
      margin: 14px 0 0;
      padding-left: 22px;
    }

    .feature-grid,
    .doc-grid {
      margin-top: 18px;
    }

    .doc-column ul,
    .feature-group ul {
      margin-top: 10px;
    }

    a {
      color: var(--accent-2);
    }

    code {
      padding: 0.15rem 0.45rem;
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.82);
      color: #dbeafe;
      font-family: "Cascadia Code", "Consolas", monospace;
    }

    .footer {
      margin-top: 18px;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      main {
        width: min(100% - 20px, 1040px);
        padding-top: 18px;
      }

      .hero,
      .section {
        border-radius: 18px;
        padding: 24px 20px;
      }

      .button {
        width: 100%;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">${project_name_short} distribution notes</div>
      <h1>${project_name_short}</h1>
      <p class="tagline">One engine, Quake III Arena and Quake Live profiles</p>
      <p class="subtitle">
        <strong>${project_name_short}</strong> combines FnQuake3 modernization and the FnQL compatibility baseline in one engine with <em>Quake III Arena</em> and <em>Quake Live</em> profiles.
      </p>
      <div class="buttons">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="docs/fntech3/COMPATIBILITY.md">Compatibility status</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="#getting-started">Getting started</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="#documentation">Documentation</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/BUILD.md">Build guide</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="LICENSE">License</a>
      </div>
      <div class="stats">
        <article class="card">
          <strong>Compatibility target</strong>
          <p>${compatibility_target}</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <strong>Base version</strong>
          <p>${base_version}</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <strong>Current build</strong>
          <p>${version}</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <strong>Tagged release format</strong>
          <p><code>${release_tag_example}</code></p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="introduction">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
        <p class="lead"><strong>${project_name_short}</strong> selects one immutable Q3 or QL profile before compatibility-sensitive startup. Both profiles use the same client and dedicated-server binaries.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="lead"><strong>Full compatibility is not yet established for either profile.</strong> Build and unit results do not replace runtime and retail-interoperability evidence. The <a href="docs/fntech3/COMPATIBILITY.md">compatibility ledger</a> records open gates and observed results.</p>
      <p class="footer">Supply your own legitimate installation. Retail modules, assets, and proprietary runtimes remain there. The inherited Windows release workflow still stages a separate closed-source Steam provider; its distribution policy requires review before a fnTech3 release can be approved.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="features">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>2. Features</h2>
        <p class="lead">Capabilities inherited from the engine baselines are being validated across both profiles.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Q3/QL compatibility work</h3>
          <p>Separate installation, module ABI, protocol, demo, filesystem, asset, and optional-service contracts. Retail QL behavior remains evidence while Q3 boundaries are integrated and tested.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Fast, modern hardware rendering</h3>
          <p>Choose between optimized <strong>GLx</strong>, <strong>Vulkan raster</strong> and <strong>Vulkan RTX</strong> renderers, with GPU-cached world geometry, optimized lightmaps, reduced rendering overhead, improved depth precision and better performance on large or demanding maps.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Modern visual upgrades</h3>
          <p>Optional HDR rendering and output, MSAA, supersampling, render scaling, anisotropic filtering, bloom, tone mapping, colour grading, high-quality dynamic lighting and shadows, motion blur, lens flares, soft particles, enhanced liquids and per-map fog.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Improved player visibility</h3>
          <p>Optional player rim lighting, stencil outlines or both, with configurable enemy, teammate, team and free-for-all colours, intensity and outline thickness. Cel shading, model outlines and world-edge outlines are also available.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Better modern hardware and OS support</h3>
          <p>SDL3-based video and input, OpenAL audio, modern graphics APIs, high-resolution and high-refresh displays, borderless/windowed/fullscreen modes, fast Alt+Enter switching, controller hotplugging and improved compatibility with current desktop systems.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Low-latency, configurable controls</h3>
          <p>Raw mouse input, Quake Live-accurate CPI scaling, signed acceleration, sensitivity caps and angle-history filtering, while retaining classic Quake3e/ioquake3 mouse styles. Modern gamepads and Unicode text input are also supported.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Modern spatial audio</h3>
          <p>OpenAL and HRTF headphone positioning, surround output, reverb, geometry-based occlusion, output-device selection, live device recovery and automatic fallback to the classic software mixer.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Major quality-of-life improvements</h3>
          <p>Scalable TTF console text, smooth scrolling, mouse selection, clipboard support, drag-and-drop editing, live command/CVar/map completion, minimize hotkeys, focus muting, lower background CPU usage and more flexible player configuration.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Better screenshots, video and streaming tools</h3>
          <p>PNG, TGA, JPEG and BMP capture, clipboard screenshots, custom filenames, camera metadata, configurable levelshots, watermarks, cubemap capture, arbitrary-resolution output and FFmpeg video piping.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Faster content handling</h3>
          <p>Quicker startup and map restarts with large PK3 libraries, raised filesystem and map limits, fast redirected downloads and automatic handling of server-required Workshop content.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Greater stability and security</h3>
          <p>Extensive Quake3e and FnQ3 bug fixes, improved memory management, lower memory usage, stronger network protection and graceful fallbacks when optional rendering, audio, WebUI or Steam functionality is unavailable.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="getting-started">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>3. Getting Started</h2>
        <p class="lead">Build the shared Windows x86 client or Linux i686 dedicated server and supply the legitimate installation for your chosen profile.</p>
      </div>
      <p>Keep <code>FnQL-pkg.fnz</code>, <code>fnql-web.pak</code>, <code>fnql_&lt;renderer&gt;_x86</code> modules, and required redistributable libraries beside <code>${executable_basename}.exe</code> and <code>${executable_basename}.ded.exe</code>. The sidecar names preserve existing loader contracts.</p>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Windows client profile selection</h3>
          <p>Use <code>+set com_gameProfile q3</code> or <code>+set com_gameProfile ql</code>, <code>+set fs_basepath "&lt;game installation&gt;"</code>, a separate writable <code>fs_homepath</code>, and <code>+set r_fullscreen 0</code> for windowed testing.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-group">
          <h3>Native Linux dedicated server</h3>
          <p>Run <code>./${executable_basename}.ded</code> with the same explicit profile and isolated home-path options. The QL server loads retail <code>qagamei386.so</code>; native Linux clients cannot load Win32-only QL client/UI modules.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="footer">Automatic selection needs unambiguous installation evidence. The selected profile is immutable. Startup, module loading, demos, play, and retail interoperability must pass the profile-specific gates before release compatibility is claimed.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="documentation">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>4. Documentation</h2>
        <p class="lead">Start with the player guides for setup and tuning. Build, compatibility, and implementation details live in the technical references.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="doc-grid">
        <article class="doc-column">
          <h3>Player guides</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/DISPLAY.md">Display Guide</a> for renderers, display modes, HDR, scaling, anti-aliasing, bloom, lighting, shadows, fog, liquids, lens flares, and motion blur.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/RTX.md">RTX Renderer Guide</a> for requirements, renderer selection, fallback behavior, safe settings, and troubleshooting.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/VISUALS.md">Visuals Guide</a> for player highlighting, colours, cel shading, and outlines.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/ASPECT_CORRECTION.md">Aspect Handling Guide</a> for the retail WebUI, menus, and cinematics.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/AUDIO.md">Audio Guide</a> for devices, HRTF, spatial effects, fallback behavior, and troubleshooting.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/CONSOLE.md">Console Guide</a> for layout, scaling, completion, clipboard use, and mouse interaction.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/SCREENSHOTS.md">Screenshot Guide</a> for formats, filenames, metadata, levelshots, watermarks, and cubemaps.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/releases">FnQL baseline release history</a> for historical changelogs and downloads; these are not fnTech3 releases.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="doc-column">
          <h3>Technical and build docs</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/BUILD.md">Build Guide</a> for compiling fnTech3 locally.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/GLX.md">GLx Renderer Guide</a> for the default OpenGL-lineage renderer, diagnostics, and troubleshooting.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/fnql/INPUT_COMPATIBILITY.md">Input Compatibility Notes</a> for retail mouse math, text input, controllers, and legacy profiles.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/fnql/WEBUI_BACKEND.md">WebUI Backend Notes</a> for retail resources, platform boundaries, overlay order, and fallbacks.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/fnql/STEAM_PROVIDER.md">Steam Provider Notes</a> for the open loader ABI, provider distribution, and runtime policy.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/fnql/RTX_RENDERER.md">RTX Renderer Contract</a> for the Quake Live ABI boundary, conservative defaults, and runtime validation.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/themuffinator/FnQL/blob/main/docs/fnql/TECHNICAL.md">Technical Notes</a> for repository structure, release flow, compatibility workflow, and maintainer conventions.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="credits">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>5. Credits</h2>
        <p class="lead">fnTech3 combines FnQuake3 and FnQL with the id Software, ioquake3, and Quake3e engine lineage. QLSRP provides behavioral and ABI evidence for independently written implementation work.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="lead">Additional compatibility and feature work draws from projects and references such as <a href="https://bitbucket.org/CPMADevs/cnq3">CNQ3</a>, <a href="https://github.com/zturtleman/spearmint">Spearmint</a>, <a href="https://github.com/brugal/wolfcamql">WolfcamQL</a>, Luigi Auriemma's <a href="https://aluigi.altervista.org/papers.htm#qldec">qldec</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/Paril/DarkMatter-Q2">DarkMatter-Q2</a>.</p>
      <p class="footer">See the full upstream chain and acknowledgements in <a href="CREDITS.md">CREDITS.md</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
